     "type": "concept",
     "title": "Who Was Lucilius?",
     "content": "**Gaius Lucilius Junior** was a real person — a friend of Seneca's, somewhat younger, a Roman knight (**eques**) serving as **procurator** (financial governor) of **Sicily** when the Letters were written. He was a poet, a man of literary tastes, and — crucially — someone in the middle of a successful public career, with all its temptations.\n\nLucilius matters because he is **not yet committed**. He is interested in Stoicism but still wavering. He owns property, holds office, enjoys his wine. Seneca writes to a man who could go either way — toward deeper philosophy or back into the pursuit of status.\n\nThis is why the Letters work as a curriculum. Lucilius is a stand-in for **anyone in the middle of life** who feels the pull of something deeper but cannot quite let go of the surface. Seneca does not lecture him. He coaches him, gently — letter by letter, idea by idea — toward the practice of the philosophy.\n\nWhen we read the Letters, we are reading Lucilius's mail. Which means we are also Lucilius. Which means **the curriculum is for us**.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">LUCILIUS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">The friend on the threshold</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"180\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"235\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">WHO HE WAS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"280\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Roman eques and poet</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"315\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Procurator of Sicily, c. 62 CE</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"380\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"435\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">WHERE HE STOOD</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"480\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Interested in Stoicism</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"515\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Not yet committed — could go either way</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"580\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"635\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">WHY HE MATTERS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"680\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">The everyman of the Letters</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"715\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">A stand-in for anyone mid-life, mid-career</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"800\" width=\"700\" height=\"100\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"845\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"22\">Lucilius is reading these letters.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"875\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">So are you.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "The friend who became every reader"
     }
