     "explanation": "Seneca explicitly targets the \"I'll get to it later\" mindset in Letter 1. Deferral is the textbook case of **effluit** — letting time flow out through our own carelessness. *\"Dum differtur, vita transcurrit\"* — *while we are postponing, life is running by*. The very busyness we use as an excuse is the proof that we have ceded our hours to other masters.",
