     "explanation": "Letter 26's practice is the **Stoic examen** — a short, honest nightly review of the day. The questions are precise: what virtue did I gain? what evil did I refrain from? what weakness showed? It is neither punitive (no guilt-mongering) nor dismissive (no denial). It is an audit. The same practice was later adopted by **Marcus Aurelius** in his Meditations and, much later, by **Ignatius of Loyola** in his spiritual exercises.",
