     "explanation": "Seneca draws the line at the choice to sustain and cultivate grief rather than at the involuntary first pang, which he considers natural even for the wise. He explicitly rejects the idea that the sage feels nothing, calling that position inhuman; his target is prolonged, self-indulgent mourning that neither benefits the dead nor serves the living.",
